    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nWhen not using web devicons, I think it would be nice to allow user to configure the icons it uses for directories and files, so I could use, for instance, `>` for directories and empty string for files. Currently the defaults are hard coded in the `make_icon_getter` function, or at least that's what I understood from the code.\r\n\r\nI did some coding and got a working version, I made a `icons` field in config and the defaults are the ones previously hard coded in `make_icon_getter`. If it is of your interest, I could open a PR. Otherwise, we can just close this.\r\n\r\nWhat do you think? (:",
